35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The readmission trial worked, but the shared nursing round failed due to logistics.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The booking system misses unrecorded work, and our rooms and parking are already full.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The joint clinic closed because neither department wanted the burden. Data agreements take too long.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Nursing vacancies are high, and agency costs are rising. Midwifery has slack, though.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The budget is down a quarter, and off-site visits earn no tariff. We must be careful.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, if off-site visits earn nothing, how do we justify a home follow-up team?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, the data agreement delay is a major bottleneck for any external coordination.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, exactly. If we cannot link records, coordination is just paperwork.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, the midwifery slack is interesting. Could we use that for perinatal support?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Yumi, if it is on-site, it bills at the standard rate. That is the key.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"The readmission data suggests home visits work, but the funding model is weak.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,The physical constraints are severe. A day unit might fit better than home visits.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,Chronic care coordination requires data links we do not have. It is risky.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,Perinatal support uses existing midwifery slack and is on-site. It seems viable.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,The budget is tight. We need a program that generates revenue on-site.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I am leaning towards the perinatal service. It uses available staff and is on-site.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"I agree. The day unit is also good, but perinatal fits the current staffing better.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I am concerned about the data issues for chronic care. Perinatal seems safer.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I support the perinatal service. It leverages the midwifery slack effectively.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,The financials support an on-site program. Perinatal looks like the best choice.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
